  "avoidBefore": "all",
  "energy": "Long periods at high heart rate under heat and g-force, so drivers need a strong aerobic base plus neck and trunk endurance.",
  "summary": "Racing loads the neck, trunk and forearms for the whole race, while heat and high heart rates wear down concentration. The plan builds neck strength and endurance, grip and an aerobic base, and keeps hard sessions away from race weekends.",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "claim": "Neck strength is the main sport-specific adaptation in Formula 1 drivers, who race at high heart rates under heat stress.",
      "source": "Tyler et al. 2026, British Journal of Sports Medicine",
      "url": "https://bjsm.bmj.com/content/60/9/649"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Open-wheel racing produces about 4-5 g in braking and cornering, with upper-body and neck fatigue a prominent response.",
      "source": "Review of physiological responses to open-wheeled racing 2021, Edith Cowan University",
      "url": "https://lida.sport-iat.de/ta/Record/4068839?lng=en"
    }
  ],
